From: Hampus Hellsberg <hampushellsberg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] esim.saip: derive nb_rec from efFileSize when the descriptor omits it

File.from_template copies the template's record count, so a profile whose
fileDescriptor carries no number of records but declares a larger
efFileSize kept the template default (EF.MSISDN: one 24-byte record from
FilesUsimOptional against a 68-byte, two-record file). ETSI TS 102 222
sizes a linear fixed EF as record length times record count; when the
descriptor is silent the declared size is the count.
---
 pySim/esim/saip/__init__.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/pySim/esim/saip/__init__.py
+++ b/pySim/esim/saip/__init__.py
@@ -337,8 +337,8 @@ class File:
                 if fd_dec['record_len']:
                     self.rec_len = fd_dec['record_len']
                 if efFileSize:
-                    if self.rec_len and self.nb_rec == None:
-                        # compute the number of records from file size and record length
+                    if self.rec_len and not fd_dec['num_of_rec']:
+                        # the profile's size wins over a template count when the descriptor omits it
                         self.nb_rec = self._file_size // self.rec_len
                 if fdb_dec['structure'] == 'linear_fixed':
                     self.file_type = 'LF'
